section: identity
title: Identity and permissions
about: |
  The cloud account of the cluster, the role or the key behind it, and the permissions the build
  needs of it. Palette checks that a role can be assumed and that policies exist, not that the role
  can build the cluster type.
rules:
- id: vsphere-account-endpoint
  title: The vCenter server of the cloud account is a host name with no scheme
  engines:
  - vsphere
  tier: static
  severity: fail
  status: source
  when: .account != null
  what: |
    Palette refuses a `vcenterServer` that starts with `http` or `https`: "Vcenter
    server name should not start with http or https". The account converter refuses a value
    that is not a server endpoint. The account validate route, `POST /v1/clouds/vsphere/account/validate`,
    needs the password, and the world holds it redacted, so strata-preflight cannot call it. The
    route through the PCG, `POST /v1/overlords/vsphere/{uid}/account/validate`, needs it too.
  check:
    kind: static
    expr: |
      (.account.spec.vcenterServer // "") as $v
      | if $v == "" then ["the vSphere account \(.account.metadata.name) has no vcenterServer"]
        elif ($v | test("^https?://")) then ["vcenterServer \($v) starts with a scheme: Palette refuses it with \"Vcenter server name should not start with http or https\""]
        elif ($v | test("^[A-Za-z0-9.-]+(:[0-9]+)?$") | not) then ["vcenterServer \($v) is not a host name or an address"]
        else [] end
  reproduce:
  - 'curl -sk -o /dev/null -w ''%{http_code}\n'' https://{{ .account.spec.vcenterServer // "<vcenter>" }}/sdk   # from the PCG; vCenter answers on 443'
  evidence:
  - kind: source
    note: refuses a server that starts with http or https, then opens a session
  - kind: source
    note: Palette refuses an empty vcenterServer, and a value that is not a server endpoint
  tests:
  - fault: fixtures/vsphere/vcenter-https.json
    clean: fixtures/vsphere/clean.json
- id: maas-account-endpoint
  title: The MAAS API endpoint of the cloud account is a URL with the /MAAS path
  engines:
  - maas
  tier: static
  severity: fail
  status: source
  when: .account != null
  what: |
    The MAAS account holds `apiEndpoint` and `apiKey`. The docs show the endpoint as
    `http://10.1.1.1:5240/MAAS`; the API lives under `/MAAS/api/2.0/`. Palette refuses an endpoint
    it cannot parse. The account validate route, `POST /v1/clouds/maas/account/validate`, needs
    the key, and the world holds it redacted, so strata-preflight cannot call it. The check reads
    the shape of the endpoint. The PCG, or Palette, must reach it; the reproduce line asks the
    version route.
  check:
    kind: static
    expr: |
      (.account.spec.apiEndpoint // "") as $e
      | if $e == "" then ["the MAAS account \(.account.metadata.name) has no apiEndpoint"]
        elif ($e | test("^https?://[^/]+(/MAAS)?/?$") | not) then ["apiEndpoint \($e) is not http(s)://host:port/MAAS: the docs show http://10.1.1.1:5240/MAAS, and Palette refuses an endpoint it cannot parse"]
        elif ($e | test("/MAAS/?$") | not) then ["apiEndpoint \($e) has no /MAAS path; the MAAS API lives under /MAAS/api/2.0/"]
        else [] end
  reproduce:
  - 'curl -s -o /dev/null -w ''%{http_code}\n'' {{ (.account.spec.apiEndpoint // "http://<maas>:5240/MAAS") | rtrimstr("/") }}/api/2.0/version/   # from the PCG, or from Palette with a direct connection; 200 or 401 means the endpoint answers'
  fix:
    owner: palette
    text: Call the account validate route at cluster create, through the PCG of the account.
  evidence:
  - kind: doc
    ref: https://docs.spectrocloud.com/clusters/pcg/deploy-pcg/maas/
    note: MAAS Server URL, example http://10.1.1.1:5240/MAAS
  - kind: source
    note: Palette checks the endpoint, then checks the credentials through the PCG
  tests:
  - fault: fixtures/maas/endpoint-bad.json
    clean: fixtures/maas/clean.json
- id: aks-aad-profile
  title: An AKS AAD profile names an admin group
  engines:
  - aks
  tier: static
  severity: fail
  status: source
  what: |
    With `cloudConfig.aadProfile` set, the provider reads `managed` and `adminGroupObjectIDs`
    with no nil check, and the CRD marks both required. The AKS pack refuses an empty group list
    with "minimum required AdminGroupObjectIDs is 1". With `disableLocalAccounts` in the pack,
    the service principal of the cloud account must be in one of the groups, or nobody can
    administer the cluster. The groups cannot change after the create.
  check:
    kind: static
    expr: |
      (.entity.spec.cloudConfig.aadProfile // null) as $a
      | if $a == null then []
        else [ ( if ($a | has("managed") | not) then "aadProfile.managed is not set: the provider reads it with no nil check, and the CRD marks it required" else empty end ),
               ( if (($a.adminGroupObjectIDs // []) | length) == 0 then "aadProfile.adminGroupObjectIDs is empty: the AKS pack refuses it with \"minimum required AdminGroupObjectIDs is 1\", and the groups cannot change after the create" else empty end ) ]
        end
  fix:
    owner: palette
    text: Check the AAD profile in the AKS validate route.
  evidence:
  - kind: source
    note: '"minimum required AdminGroupObjectIDs is 1"; the cluster config fields are dereferenced without a nil check'
  - kind: doc
    ref: https://docs.spectrocloud.com/clusters/public-cloud/azure/enable-iam-features-aks/enable-microsoft-entra-id-aks/
    note: adminGroupObjectIDs is required when managed is true; the groups cannot be changed after cluster creation
  tests:
  - fault: fixtures/aks/aad-no-groups.json
    clean: fixtures/aks/aad-clean.json
